# Architecture Rules

## Goal

Ship a working **iMessage expert-hiring agent** without creating unmaintainable code. Every feature should be easy to extend or delete.

Read `agents/rules/product.mdc` for product loop and channel constraints.

## File size

- **Never** create 400+ line files with multiple responsibilities
- One exported function/component per file when practical
- Compose in `index.ts` / `index.tsx` in the same subdirectory

## Layering

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| Routes | `app/` | Page composition, minimal logic |
| API / webhooks | `app/api/` | HTTP handlers, validation, call libs/db |
| UI (lander) | `components/lander/` | Marketing UI, hardcoded data |
| UI (app) | `components/app/` | Operator / dashboard UI |
| UI primitives | `components/ui/` | shadcn only |
| Dynamic UI | `components/dynamic/` | Wallet provider + widget wrappers |
| CRUD | `db/<domain>/index.ts` | Supabase reads/writes |
| Logic | `libs/<domain>/` | Business functions (Linq, Terac, Dynamic, agent) |
| Schemas | `utils/schema/` | Zod schemas + inferred types |
| Tests | `tests/` | Mirror source tree |

## Domain folders (prefer these)

| Domain | `libs/` | `db/` | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|-------|
| Messaging | `libs/linq/` | `db/chats/` (when needed) | Webhook ingest → agent turn |
| Agent | `libs/agent/` | — | Intent parsing, tool routing, reply drafting |
| Experts | `libs/terac/` | `db/jobs/` / `db/opportunities/` | Never launch without explicit confirm |
| Payments | `libs/dynamic/` | `db/payments/` | Coordinate escrow/payout state |
| Auth (web) | `libs/auth/` | `db/users/` | Supabase and/or Dynamic |

## Data

- **Landers**: hardcoded const data in component subdirs — no DB calls
- **App / agent**: fetch via server components, server actions, or API routes
- **Never** put CRUD in React components
- **Never** call Linq/Terac/Dynamic SDKs from client components (except Dynamic React provider/widget)

## Types

- Segment interfaces by domain in `lib/types/<domain>.ts` or colocate with schemas
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- No enums — use `as const` maps

## Design system

- Base theme: shadcn neutral black/white (light + `.dark`)
- **Accent**: `--brand-accent` in `globals.css` + `lib/constants/branding.ts`
- Fonts: `.font-primary` (body/UI), `.font-secondary` (headlines/display) — two fonts only
- **Styling**: read `styling.mdc` — props over `className`, global UI changes in `components/ui/`

## Testing

- Add tests when implementing a feature
- Mirror path: `libs/linq/foo.ts` → `tests/libs/linq/foo.test.ts`

## Dynamic design (UI)

- Build reusable layout primitives before page-specific UI
- Prefer composition over one-off styles
- Use Framer Motion for meaningful transitions, not decoration everywhere
